    <div class="opening" id="begin">
      <p class="eyebrow">A NECESSARY STARTING POINT</p>
      <h2>There is no single Native American story.</h2>
      <p>Long before the United States existed, North America was home to hundreds of distinct Indigenous nations and communities. They developed their own languages, systems of government, trade networks, farming traditions, technologies, art, and ways of understanding the world. Their histories were connected through diplomacy, commerce, migration, conflict, and family relationships — but they were never one single culture.</p>
      <p class="ru">Задолго до появления США Северная Америка была домом для множества самостоятельных народов. У них были собственные языки, формы управления, торговые связи, технологии, искусство и традиции. Их истории пересекались, но единой «индейской культуры» никогда не существовало.</p>
    </div>

    <figure class="hero-figure">
      <img src="/american-english-method/images/history/native-peoples/Портрет вождя на фоне прерий.png" alt="Illustrative portrait of a Native American man wearing richly decorated Plains-style feathered regalia" loading="eager" />
